## =============================================================================
## .github/dependabot.yml.template — automatic dependency update pull requests
## =============================================================================
## GUIDE STEP   0.5 (turn on Dependabot)
## PURPOSE      Dependabot is a GitHub service that checks weekly whether newer
##              versions (and especially security fixes) exist for:
##                - Python packages (from pyproject.toml / uv.lock),
##                - Docker base images (Dockerfile.platform, deploy/caddy/Dockerfile),
##                - the GitHub Actions used by the workflows,
##              and opens one pull request per update. CI then tests each
##              update before you merge it.
## WHY THE .template SUFFIX
##              Kept consistent with the workflow templates: nothing in .github
##              becomes active until you decide. Activate by uncommenting and
##              renaming to dependabot.yml.
## USED BY      GitHub.
## WHY          Guide §2.2 dependency hygiene: vulnerabilities are found in
##              dependencies all the time; small, frequent, tested updates are
##              far safer than rare big ones.
## ACTIVATE     Uncomment, rename, push; check "Insights -> Dependency graph ->
##              Dependabot" on GitHub. Note: Dependabot's support for uv lock
##              files is ecosystem "uv"; if your GitHub plan/version does not
##              offer it yet, use "pip" (it reads pyproject.toml).
## =============================================================================

